b) LaTeX is independent of Omega  and so you should be able to parse =
LICR as
well in Omega if Omega is running with LaTeX on top.

now of course both are lies to some extend, so try again:

 - point a) above is not true if you plug something on top of LaTeX to =
bypass
   its internal handling and replace it with something else, like part =
of the
   language support for omega that is currently being worked on by =
Javier.
   question however is whether this will lead in the long term to =
anything
   useful for both sides --- i doubt it.

 - point b) depends on how Omega wants to make use of those patterns. =
does it
